@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 19 and 20"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.16.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch19ch20-lineage/1.16.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch19ch20_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.16.0 (2026-11-18): the lineage stays open (the owner asked why a lineage with unfinished work would be closed; the closure report of 2026-11-16 is withdrawn and not committed). Root cause of the page-test browser crash found: a defect in the page template, not the test tool. Chapter 20 page 9.99.0 on template 9.53.5 passes the whole page test; the Chapter 19 page carries the same defect and the WHO/WHERE/WHEN labels and is reopened for a rebuild."@en .

ex:TK8_BuildPage_Ch20 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Page 9.99.0 (03-materials/ch20/page/sen0414_ch20_page_v9_99_0.html, template 9.53.5) replaces 9.98.0. Two defects of 9.98.0 are corrected: (1) the page template started the Oxigraph WebAssembly module twice at once when tabs were opened quickly (ensureGraph, ensureChunks and ensureEmbed had no in-flight guard, and the worker initialised the module on every graph message); the second start corrupted the module heap (Rust dlmalloc panic, then a renderer SEGV) and crashed the tab. Found by capturing the browser's own error output at the crash and reproducing it with a 114-step tab loop (9.98.0 crashed in 6 of 6 runs; 9.99.0 survived 5 of 5). Earlier registers (1.12.0, 1.13.0, 1.15.0) recorded this as a harness defect with unknown cause: that attribution was wrong, the page was at fault. (2) the research A-box examples used an err helper that evaluated text; the page test's check for evaluated code found the word eval in the page. A-box 1.0.4 (maker 1.1.0, 08-tooling/ch20-page/abox_lambda_free_make_v1_1_0.py) writes each err(lambda: X) as a small def before the statement, 57 of 57 results equal to the originals, 0 lambda and 0 eval left." .
ex:TK8_BuildVerify_Ch20 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Logs in 08-tooling/ch20-page/logs_v9_99_0: page test 9.39.0 (unchanged) ran to the end: 412 features passed, 0 failed, including the phone and tablet layouts, later-pane accessibility, light theme, sideways scroll and the release step; material check 8 of 8 pass; manifest self-check pass; story layout 19 of 19 pass. STILL NOT VERIFIED: the verification is by the same agent that built the material (not independent); the reviewed conditions (academician, faculty reviewer, undergraduate reader) are not recorded; the declared deck-standard measure (check 1.0.0) contradicts the 2026-11-14 rulings and is not met; the links were not re-opened in this session." .
ex:ST8_BuildCh20 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck 2.0.0, page 9.99.0 and their checks done; the open points are listed on the verify task." .
ex:TK8_BuildPage_Ch19 backlog:hasState backlog:InProgress ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Reopened by change management on this lineage: page 9.97.1 was built on template 9.53.3, which (1) still prints the WHO/WHERE/WHEN labels in the Stories tab, against the owner's rulings, and (2) has the Oxigraph double-start defect that crashed the page test. The page is rebuilt on template 9.53.5 as 9.97.2 (own version over 9.97.1)." .
ex:ST8_BuildCh19 backlog:hasState backlog:InProgress ; backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck 2.2.0 done; the page is being rebuilt on template 9.53.5 (labels, tab crash); its page test must then run to the end." .
